# Production deploys — GitHub CD only

All production deploys to `100.71.124.8` (policy tracker) MUST go through the **GitHub Actions CD pipeline** (push to `main` → `.github/workflows/deploy.yml`).

## Do

- Commit and **push to `main`** when prod needs updated code
- Verify the GitHub Actions deploy workflow succeeded
- Use prod helper scripts that **only read logs or run one-off jobs inside the existing container** (e.g. `docker compose exec scheduler python scripts/...`) when the user asks for operational tasks — not as a substitute for shipping code

## Do NOT (unless the operating user explicitly says otherwise)

- Run `./deploy/deploy.sh` or manual rsync/SSH deploys
- Run `scripts/wsl-deploy-remote.sh` directly from a dev machine to push code
- `docker cp` hot-patched scripts onto prod as a deploy strategy
- Tell the user "deploy is done" after a manual rsync while CI is the source of truth

## When manual deploy is allowed

Only when the user **explicitly** requests a manual deploy in the current conversation (e.g. "run deploy.sh", "manual deploy now", "rsync to prod").

## Rationale

Manual deploys can diverge from `main` (rsync full working tree, uncommitted files, missing excludes). GitHub CD is the canonical path to prod.
